From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:40:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: tty-sdio: configure the Bluetooth core from the kernel (PSKEY/RF/enable)

The UWE5622 BT core comes up unconfigured and disabled. Until now the
closed-source hciattach_opi read bt_configure_pskey.ini and
bt_configure_rf.ini, sent the vendor commands 0xFCA0 (PSKEY, 176 B), 0xFCA2
(RF parameters, 252 B) and 0xFCA1 (enable) over /dev/ttyBT0 and then set the
HCI line discipline.

Do the vendor part in the driver when rfkill powers the core on
(bluetooth_set_power -> start_marlin -> sprd_bt_init), so that stock BlueZ
"btattach -B /dev/ttyBT0 -P h4" is all userspace needs:

- bt_init.c (new): load the two ini files with request_firmware() (root of
  /lib/firmware, fallback uwe5622/), parse "key = v1, v2, ..." lines,
  serialise the PSKEY/RF tables exactly as the vendor tool does and send them
  with hci_cmd_send_sync(). Derived from Reinerost's OpenWrt port
  (https://github.com/Reinerost/UWE5622-OpenWrt-Driver, tested on a WalnutPi
  1B with the same firmware).
- BD address: bdaddr= module parameter, else the Allwinner addr_mgt "bt"
  address (CONFIG_SUNXI_ADDR_MGT, the same source hciattach_opi reads via
  /sys/class/addr_mgt/addr_bt, same call unisocwifi uses for the WLAN MAC),
  else the ini default. Stored LSB first in the PSKEY (HCI order).
- hci_cmd_send_sync(): report transport errors, timeouts and non-zero HCI
  status to the caller (it returned 0 unconditionally), pad the frame to the
  SDIO 4-byte alignment like the tty write path does.
- Idempotent: "rfkill unblock" is repeated by systemd-rfkill and the attach
  service; the firmware is configured once per power-up, the latch is cleared
  on block and on the firmware reset notifier.
- On init failure the core is powered down again and the error is returned,
  so the rfkill switch stays blocked and userspace can retry.
- New CONFIG_TTY_OVERY_SDIO_BT_VENDOR_INIT (default y) and module parameter
  vendor_init (default Y): vendor_init=0 restores the previous behaviour for
  people who want to keep the vendor hciattach.
- The "mtty bt is closed abnormally" error for events that arrive while the
  tty is closed is now expected (they are consumed by woble_data_recv) and
  demoted to pr_debug.
- rfkill registered last in mtty_probe(): an early "rfkill unblock" (systemd-rfkill)
  must find the SDIO channels and TX semaphore initialised.

The HCI park-mode quirk is not needed here: armbian/firmware already clears
the park bit in feature_set (PR #154).

(dkms.conf gets the same CONFIG_TTY_OVERY_SDIO_BT_VENDOR_INIT=y in the upstream
copy; it is not part of the tree Armbian injects.)
Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622 (git-am
copy: harness/research/uwe5622-upstream/0004-*.patch). Applies on top of
the f88cd0d pin.
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
